0result.sql uses correct logic but is a bit more convoluted;  
1result.sql is logically wrong because it builds the streak‑id on a row set that still contains multiple rows per date, so the row_number() counter grows faster than the calendar days and can split / merge streaks incorrectly whenever a date has several city rows.  
2result.sql keeps only DISTINCT dates before computing the streak identifier, then cleanly picks one city per date and produces the wanted two streaks (shortest = 2 days, longest = 13 days) with properly‑capitalised city names. It therefore meets every requirement with the simplest, safest approach.

```plaintext
2result.sql
```